---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---
<Layout
  title="Hanfu Experience in China: City-by-City Rental & Photoshoot Guide"
  description="Where to wear Hanfu in China: rental prices, best photoshoot spots, and practical tips for Xi'an, Hangzhou, Beijing, Suzhou, Chengdu, and Luoyang. Real ranges, not vague advice."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.dresses-hanfu.com/travel/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Travel", url: "/travel" }]}
>
  <SiteHeader active="/travel" />
  <main>
    <article>
      <section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;"><a href="/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Home</a> &rsaquo; Travel</p>
          <h1>Hanfu Experience in China: City-by-City Guide</h1>
          <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:1.5rem;line-height:1.55;">
            The best way to experience Hanfu is to wear it where it belongs — in China, in front of a thousand-year-old wall or a misty lake. This guide covers six cities, what a rental actually costs, the best spots to shoot, and how to get from "want to" to "wearing it."
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container">
          <h2>Pick Your City</h2>
          <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">Six cities, six different Hanfu moods. Rentals run roughly 60–350 RMB per day everywhere listed.</p>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <a href="/travel/xian/" class="vs-card" style="display:block;color:inherit;">
              <h3>Xi'an</h3>
              <p>The ultimate Hanfu city — City Wall, Tang Paradise, sunset magic. Rentals 100–200 RMB.</p>
              <span style="display:inline-block;margin-top:0.75rem;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-accent);">Read the guide →</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/travel/hangzhou/" class="vs-card" style="display:block;color:inherit;">
              <h3>Hangzhou</h3>
              <p>West Lake — mist, bridges, cherry blossoms. The most-photographed Hanfu spot. Rentals 150–300 RMB.</p>
              <span style="display:inline-block;margin-top:0.75rem;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-accent);">Read the guide →</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/travel/beijing/" class="vs-card" style="display:block;color:inherit;">
              <h3>Beijing</h3>
              <p>Forbidden City, Summer Palace, snowy palace shots. Rentals 150–350 RMB.</p>
              <span style="display:inline-block;margin-top:0.75rem;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-accent);">Read the guide →</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/travel/suzhou/" class="vs-card" style="display:block;color:inherit;">
              <h3>Suzhou</h3>
              <p>Classical gardens, fewer crowds, silk capital. Rentals 120–250 RMB.</p>
              <span style="display:inline-block;margin-top:0.75rem;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-accent);">Read the guide →</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/travel/chengdu/" class="vs-card" style="display:block;color:inherit;">
              <h3>Chengdu</h3>
              <p>Jinli and Kuanzhai lanes, a young Hanfu scene, pandas nearby. Rentals 80–200 RMB.</p>
              <span style="display:inline-block;margin-top:0.75rem;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-accent);">Read the guide →</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/travel/luoyang/" class="vs-card" style="display:block;color:inherit;">
              <h3>Luoyang</h3>
              <p>Buddhist grottoes and temple backdrops — the cheapest, least crowded option. Rentals 60–150 RMB.</p>
              <span style="display:inline-block;margin-top:0.75rem;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-accent);">Read the guide →</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>What You'll Actually Pay</h2>
          <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
            <table class="size-ref-table" style="margin-top:1rem;">
              <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Typical Range</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><strong>Hanfu rental (24h)</strong></td><td>60–350 RMB (~$8–48 USD)</td><td>Hairstyling often included; deposit 200–500 RMB</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Hairstyle / makeup</strong></td><td>Often bundled, or 50–150 RMB extra</td><td>Complex crowns cost more</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Photographer (1–2h)</strong></td><td>300–800 RMB (~$40–110 USD)</td><td>20–50 edited photos, delivered within 24h</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Attraction tickets</strong></td><td>30–120 RMB per site</td><td>Some rental shops offer combo deals</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:0.75rem;">Book photographers 1–2 days ahead in peak season (spring and autumn).</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>Before You Go</h2>
          <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--color-muted);font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.8;">
            <li><strong>Book ahead in high season</strong> — spring and autumn weekends sell out, especially in Xi'an and Beijing.</li>
            <li><strong>Bring your passport</strong> — most shops require it as ID for the rental deposit.</li>
            <li><strong>Know the collar rule</strong> — right over left. See <a href="/guides/how-to-wear/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">How to Wear Hanfu</a> for the full sequence.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the return window</strong> — most rentals are 24 hours; returning late usually costs a half-day fee.</li>
            <li><strong>Language</strong> — major-city shops have English-speaking staff or translation apps. Outside peaks, a phrase like "租汉服" (rent Hanfu) on your phone helps.</li>
          </ul>

          <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding:2rem;background:var(--color-accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);">
            <p style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);">Next Steps</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:1rem;">
              <a href="/travel/xian/" class="btn btn-outline">Xi'an Guide</a>
              <a href="/guides/how-to-wear/" class="btn btn-outline">How to Wear Hanfu</a>
              <a href="/guides/sizing/" class="btn btn-outline">Hanfu Size Guide</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
